        "knowledge_point": "Completing a Table of Signs",
        "problem": "What are the missing entries in the sign table below?\n\n|  | $(-\\infty ,-2)$ | $(-2,8)$ | $(8,\\infty )$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x+2$ | $-$ | {{field-1}} | $+$ |\n| $x-8$ | $-$ | {{field-2}} | $+$ |\n| $(x+2)(x-8)$ | $+$ | {{field-3}} | $+$ |",
        "worked_solution": "On the interval $(-2,8),$ we can choose a test point ${x}_{1}=0.$ Then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+2 & =0+2=(+), \\\\ x-8 & =0-8=(-), \\\\ (x+2)(x-8) & =(+)\\times (-)=(-),\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we fill in the table as follows:\n\n|  | $(-\\infty ,-2)$ | $(-2,8)$ | $(8,\\infty )$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x+2$ | $-$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| $x-8$ | $-$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n| $(x+2)(x-8)$ | $+$ | $-$ | $+$ |",
